#
# Intent: Higher or Lower, Reversi, Dice Poker, Battleship-lite, Pong, Flyer, Balance and Maze had a finished core and screen but were not in the games list. They are now kinds of the grid game
#   engine: id, English and Spanish titles, touches, the unit's move, sounds, best score, the shared game-over screen in the household language with its tone table, and the 60 s result hold.
#   Balance and Maze read the lean (maipai_games_tilt_analog) only while they run. Games never move the head. The list and start tools name the new ids.
# Placement: unit (body half; the existing own-LLM and Home game tools list games by these ids).
# Upstream: none (MaiPai code only).
# Check after a flash: Games list shows the eight new games; each starts, takes touch (Balance and Maze: tilt), ends on the game-over screen and saves a best score; memory gate holds with a game running.
# Kconfig: none (rides on the grid games switch).
# Memory cost: nothing while no game runs; while one runs, its object tree and state (measure each on the bench with heap checks).

